<newsitem itemid="86450" id="root" date="1996-09-30" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Northern Leisure yr pretax profit up 46 pct.</title>
<headline>Northern Leisure yr pretax profit up 46 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>53 weeks to August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.7		    vs 8.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.25		   vs 2.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 4.25		   vs 4.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.51		   vs 3.77</p>
<p> Turnover		   21.9		   vs 17.2</p>
<p>NOTE - The results are for 53 weeks compared to 52 weeks in the last financial year. Commenting on the year ahead, Northern said it saw profits for the year to August 31 1997 being &quot;materially greater&quot; than 1996 due to better trading conditions.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 5.6		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.6		    vs 1.9</p>
<p> Tax			  0.78		   vs 0.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		  4.7		    vs 3.4</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 12  Ex-div date		November 4</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
